        "category_id":  "6",
        "name":  "Singhasari Museum",
        "description":  "As the name suggests, this museum exhibits a collection of historical items that are heritage from the Singasari Kingdom, one of the largest kingdoms in Indonesia. This kingdom was also known as the Tumapel Kingdom, adhered to Hindu-Buddhist beliefs, and is located at Singhasari Residence Housing, Klampok Village, Singasari District, Malang Regency.\nWhen visiting this museum, you will find approximately 345 historical artifacts displayed in an exhibition space of 3,000 square meters. Some artifacts from the Singasari Kingdom that you can see at the Singhasari Museum include Mahisha, Mahakal, Prajna Paramita, Durga Singasari Style, and Ganesha.",
        "location":  "Singhasari Residence Housing, Klampok Village, Singasari District, Malang Regency",
        "latitude":  "-7.8879",
        "longitude":  "112.6664",
        "created_at":  "2026-09-04T00:00:00.000000Z",
