        "destination_id":  "2",
        "category_id":  "6",
        "name":  "Panji Museum",
        "description":  "Panji Museum is a museum that displays a collection of artifacts related to the legend of Panji Asmorobangun and Dewi Sekartaji, who was a princess of the Jenggala Kingdom. Here, visitors can see a diorama of the Genter War that took place in Genter Village, Malang Regency, in ancient times involving the Singasari Kingdom and the Kediri Kingdom.\nAdditionally, Panji Museum also displays various collections of wayang puppets, masks, historical artifacts, and documentation about the City of Malang in the past. To visit this museum, you can head to Jl. Raya Bangilan Number 1, Ringin Anom, Tumpang District, Malang Regency.",
        "location":  "Jl. Raya Bangilan Number 1, Ringin Anom, Tumpang District, Malang Regency",
