        "destination_id":  "2",
        "category_id":  "6",
        "name":  "Eng An Kiong Temple",
        "description":  "Eng An Kiong Temple is a historical site located on Jl. R.E. Martadinata, Kotalama, Kedungkandang District, Malang City. This historical site is a Tridharma temple, used for worship in three faiths: Buddhism, Confucianism, and Taoism.\nThe building was established in 1825 and has been designated as a cultural heritage site. Besides serving as a place of worship, Eng An Kiong Temple has also become a destination for religious and historical tourism in Malang City. The founder of this temple was a soldier named Lieutenant Kwee Sam Hway.",
        "location":  "Jl. R.E. Martadinata, Kotalama, Kedungkandang District, Malang City",
