    {
        "id":  105,
        "destination_id":  "2",
        "category_id":  "6",
        "name":  "Brawijaya Museum",
        "description":  "Brawijaya Museum has been standing since May 4, 1968. This museum is located in front of the Malang City Public Library, precisely at Jalan Besar Ijen Number 25A, Gading Kasri, Klojen District, Malang City. When visiting this museum, you will find various collections, including military objects used in the struggle to achieve and defend the independence of the Republic of Indonesia.\nOne of the famous collections in this museum is the Death Wagon (Gerbong Maut), an iron wagon that serves as evidence of the cruelty of the Dutch colonizers. This iron wagon was used to transport dozens of Indonesian fighters from Bondowoso to Surabaya in completely sealed conditions without windows, causing many fighters to perish during the journey.",
        "location":  "Jalan Besar Ijen Number 25A, Gading Kasri, Klojen District, Malang City",
        "latitude":  "-7.9724",
        "longitude":  "112.6296",
