        "category_id":  "6",
        "name":  "Ijen District",
        "description":  "Ijen District is one of the historical areas in Malang City. In this self-contained area, there are several buildings left from the Dutch colonial era, including the Saint Theresa Cathedral Church, also known as Gereja Ijen, and Dutch-style houses. The uniqueness of this area is that the street names use the names of mountains in Indonesia, such as Ijen, Semeru, Bromo, and others. The area was built by Dutch architect Herman Thomas Karsten around 1935.",
        "location":  "Ijen District, Klojen, Malang City",
        "latitude":  "-7.9695",
