        "destination_id":  "2",
        "category_id":  "6",
        "name":  "Watugede Bathing Site",
        "description":  "Watugede Bathing Site is a bathing pool sourced from natural springs. This site is estimated to be a royal garden complex from the Majapahit Kingdom era. The site stands on a land area of 2,516 square meters. There is clear spring water gushing from beneath a tree at the edge of the pool. The spring water then flows into two pools located to the north and south. Watugede Bathing Site, discovered in 1925, has been designated as a National Cultural Heritage Site. It is located in Watugede Village, Singosari District, Malang Regency.",
        "location":  "Watugede Village, Singosari District, Malang Regency",
